      "repair_reason": "- [P1] The remaining merge gate is contributor-supplied real runtime proof, plus normal owner review of the introduced 100 MiB compatibility boundary; this is not a safe automated repair task.; Cleared: The one-file patch adds no dependency, permission, workflow, secret, or supply-chain surface and uses an existing shared filesystem API. (sha=6116fde6f7dbe71534d5dddf5be0d064e99a14fa)",
      "review_summary": "The PR changes OpenShell sandbox reads to use `root.readBytes` with hardlink rejection and a 100 MiB maximum instead of an unbounded file-handle read.\n\nPR surface: Source -3. Total -3 across 1 file.\n\nReproducibility: no. high-confidence live reproduction was supplied or run in this review. Current-main source clearly reaches an unbounded `FileHandle.readFile()` through the sandbox bridge, so the reported failure mode is source-reproducible.",
